{"name":"High Priest","hex":"#643949","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"high priest","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A clergyman with a higher function than a normal priest.","In the Bible, the male individual who was responsible for making the annual sacrifice on the Day of Atonement (Yom Kippur); always a descendant of Aaron, the older brother of Moses. See Kohen Gadol."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/high_priest"}],"entries":[{"title":"High priest","blocks":[{"text":"The term \"high priest\" usually refers either to an individual who holds the office of ruler-priest, or to one who is the head of a religious organisation."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/High_priest","wikidata":"Q3114821"},{"title":"High priest (Latter Day Saints)","blocks":[{"text":"In most denominations of the Latter Day Saint movement, a high priest is an office of the priesthood within the Melchizedek priesthood. High priests are typically more experienced leaders within the priesthood. The term derives in part from the Epistle to the Hebrews, which describes Jesus as \"a high priest after the order of Melchizedek\". Movement founder Joseph Smith ordained the first high priests on June 3, 1831."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/High_priest_(Latter_Day_Saints)","wikidata":"Q746462"},{"title":"Priest","blocks":[{"text":"A priest is a religious leader authorized to perform the sacred rituals of a religion, especially as a mediatory agent between humans and one or more deities. They also have the authority or power to administer religious rites; in particular, rites of sacrifice to, and propitiation of, a deity or deities. Their office or position is the \"priesthood\", a term which also may apply to such persons collectively. A priest may have the duty to hear confessions periodically, give marriage counseling, provide prenuptial counseling, give spiritual direction, teach catechism, or visit those confined indoors, such as the sick in hospitals and nursing homes."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/be/Priests_rome.jpg/330px-Priests_rome.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Priest","wikidata":"Q42603"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e1/Pinudjem-II.jpg/500px-Pinudjem-II.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e1/Pinudjem-II.jpg/500px-Pinudjem-II.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Pinedjem II as High Priest of Amun in Thebes. From his Book of the Dead","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3APinudjem-II.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f6/High_Priest.jpg/500px-High_Priest.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f6/High_Priest.jpg/500px-High_Priest.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Depiction of a high priest in biblical costume, end of the 17th century, orientalising representation with turban, in the collection of the Jewish Museum of Switzerland","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AHigh_Priest.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/27/Roman_Vestal_Virgin_%28150620229%29.jpg/500px-Roman_Vestal_Virgin_%28150620229%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/27/Roman_Vestal_Virgin_%28150620229%29.jpg/500px-Roman_Vestal_Virgin_%28150620229%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Vestal Virgin priestess of Ancient Rome","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ARoman_Vestal_Virgin_(150620229).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org